-- One-off translations of the site texts as they were on 2026-10-20, so French, Italian and
-- English work before the translation key is set. Existing rows (hand-written English) win.
insert into translations (hash, lang, text) values
('3389851fbf330b3812fad7cb13a7aa2f', 'en', $t$A simple alpine hut at 1200 m in the Kiental, for 1 to 6 people.$t$),
('6615d69c3c623daece68252041a88cf5', 'en', $t$The hut stands in Lengschwendi, on the sunny slope above the road into the upper Kiental. As the name says, you look out from here onto the Blüemlisalp.

Inside there is a kitchen with a wood-fired stove, a bedroom, a loft and a sitting room. Electricity comes from the solar panels, and water from the hut's own spring. If you like things simple, you'll find peace here and hiking trails right outside the door.$t$),
('7cf727efbedc22c1610a60ef139e319f', 'en', $t$- Loft: mattresses 1 × 90 cm, 1 × 140 cm and 2 × 120 cm
- Sitting room: one bed 140 × 200 cm
- You can hire bed linen or bring your own. A sleeping bag is fine too.$t$),
('d9e9710c468dfdaacb41ae2053d6a3eb', 'en', $t$- The toilet is a long-drop under the balcony, and toilet paper is provided.
- There's no fridge, but there is a 12 V cool box.
- The solar power is enough for lights and for charging phones and cameras.
- A steep wooden ladder leads up to the loft.
- How warm the water gets depends on the weather. Up to 65 °C when it's sunny.$t$),
('99ef345701e22bc27e9589da3afc6257', 'en', $t$By PostBus: line 220 from Reichenbach im Kandertal station towards Griesalp to «Kiental, Abzw. Spiggengrund», about 22 minutes. Beyond Kiental village the bus only runs from late May to mid-October, roughly every two hours. For the Friday service at 17.27 from Reichenbach you need to book by 16.00 the day before (0848 818 818).

By car: via Reichenbach into the Kiental and on towards Griesalp. The road no longer charges a toll. Where to park is in the information you get after confirmation.

Guest card: With the guest card you travel free by bus and train in the region, for example from Reichenbach to Kiental and on the chairlift up to Ramslauenen. The stretch from Kiental to Griesalp is not included.$t$),
('caae88410db8678aee4f3e72c8bb0498', 'en', $t$- The hut sleeps up to 6 people.
- Please leave the hut as you found it. Final cleaning is included in the price.$t$),
('393b64d2035212405baa10c39e6ebdf6', 'en', $t$After confirmation you'll receive a QR bill for the full amount. It is payable within 30 days, and no later than 14 days before arrival.

If you cancel up to 60 days before arrival, it costs nothing. Up to 30 days before, you pay half. After that you pay the full amount.$t$),
('8455b67662530e6e340404ae9dc1fd6e', 'en', $t$Shopping: Dorfladen Aellig, the village shop in Kiental, has bread, groceries and a post office counter, about 2 km from the hut. It delivers on Tuesday, Thursday and Saturday for CHF 5. The nearest Coop is in Reichenbach. https://www.aellig-kiental.ch

Eating out: Hotel-Restaurant Alpenruh (just over 1 km, closed Tuesday and Wednesday), Hotel Bären in Kiental, Berghaus Ramslauenen, Berggasthaus Golderli, Naturfreundehaus Gorneren and the hotels at Griesalp.

Guest card: It gives you free travel by bus from Reichenbach to Kiental, on the chairlift up to Ramslauenen, by train from Mülenen to Kandersteg and on the buses to Adelboden. The Niesenbahn, Blausee and Oeschinensee cost less. https://adelboden-lenk-kandersteg.ch/buchen/angebote/gaestekarte$t$),
('e59ce2c0217edd8d7ce4cde2015a7184', 'en', $t$Is there electricity in the hut?
Yes, solar power for lights and for charging phones and cameras. USB cables are provided.

Can I stay for just a few nights?
We rent the hut by the week, from Saturday to Saturday.

How do I get there without a car?
By PostBus 220 from Reichenbach im Kandertal to «Kiental, Abzw. Spiggengrund», about 22 minutes.

Is the tourist tax included in the price?
No, we list it separately: CHF 3 per night from age 16, half for children aged 6 to 15, plus a CHF 1 cantonal accommodation levy. In return you get the guest card with free public transport in the region.

Is bed linen provided?
You can hire it for CHF 5 per set or bring your own.$t$),
('b66cdbcc23556467ce99555c3f84834c', 'en', $t$- Sleeping bag or your own bed linen
- Head torch or torch
- Sturdy shoes for the path to the hut
- Food for the first few days
- Power bank
- Rain jacket$t$),
