('9d73ce4e972e7ee933d3a2416125a89b', 'en', $t$From Tschingel through the Griesschlucht gorge up to Griesalp, past the Pochtenfall and the Hexenkessel. A stepped path with walkways and bridges. The stream carries the most water from June to August.$t$),
('4ba1decb32cfb09057c5356aa849bd06', 'en', $t$Late May to mid-October$t$),
('a8746d6383660317048a71bebc459912', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Kiental, Tschingel» (late May to mid-October only).
Getting back: from «Griesalp, Kurhaus» by PostBus 220, or downhill on foot in about 35 minutes.
The guest card is not valid on the Kiental–Griesalp stretch.$t$),
('5c5ccaf1f76e339806af588e43d5e18a', 'en', $t$Pochtenfall: the stream plunges over a vertical rock face
Hexenkessel with a carved wooden witch
Waterfalls and plunge pools in the Griesschlucht$t$),
('e943bd0c1964dd0e4dc02341772e4be0', 'en', $t$Wet walkways and rock slabs can be slippery. Right next to the path, the PostBus runs on the steepest route in its whole network, with gradients of up to 28 %.$t$),
('dc0cddc7b34f82027392026c33fd3a90', 'en', $t$Downhill from Griesalp via the Pochtenalp, through the Griesschlucht with the Pochtenfall and Hexenkessel, past the former Tschingelsee and Bir Alperue, and via Fulbrunni to Kiental village.$t$),
('bf2060edfe2997542f296568444ec4d8', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Griesalp, Kurhaus» (late May to mid-October).
Getting back: PostBus 220 runs from «Kiental, Dorf» all year round.
The guest card is not valid on the Kiental–Griesalp stretch.$t$),
('bfac15503382ce0edbe87527d837dd2f', 'en', $t$Pochtenfall and Hexenkessel in the Griesschlucht
Former Tschingelsee, a floodplain of national importance
Fire pit at the Tschingelsee$t$),
('7f062df3a9c2a6264ee08a3ae4888717', 'en', $t$The «Kiental, Faulbrunni» stop is about 600 m from the hut as the crow flies.$t$),
('54464b9b96408a39e1aed9f91755646a', 'en', $t$Circular walk from Bir Alperue: past the former Tschingelsee, up the Bärenpfad to Gorneren and the Golderli, then via the Pochtenalp and the Wildwasserweg down to Tschingel and back.$t$),
('d08538b570d7cb102443dba9994d4af5', 'en', $t$There and back: PostBus 220 to «Kiental, Rest. Alpenruhe» (late May to mid-October).
From the hut on foot via the Guggerwäg, about 1.7 km.$t$),
('60973c53a98e7740ba15d82a9642b0da', 'en', $t$Forest path with moss-covered boulders
Carved bear at the turn-off to the Bärenpfad
Waterfall on the Bärenpfad
View from Gorneren of the Gspaltenhorn, Bütlasse and Blüemlisalp
Hexenkessel with a carved wooden witch$t$),
('87e3e056412aa0271b9e35ff8d9b411c', 'en', $t$Part of the route is marked as a mountain trail. There is public paid parking at the Tschingel nature reserve. The car park at the Alpenruh is private.$t$),
('d5877043f03a3748f9be24d803cbffa7', 'en', $t$Themed trail about the cuckoo from Ramslauenen through Lengschwendi, right past the hut, to Bir Alperue. With the guest card the chairlift up is free.$t$),
('a4a54c25b61a587c9babf93e89d43a52', 'en', $t$May to October, while the chairlift is running$t$),
('485eb720e38ae7e47b005a3b53b11cb6', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Kiental, Ramslauenen», then 15 minutes up by chairlift, free with the guest card.
Getting back: from «Kiental, Rest. Alpenruhe» by PostBus 220 (late May to mid-October), otherwise on foot to Kiental in about 1 hour.$t$),
('31348f05662f39311fe6ad15b29aeb80', 'en', $t$Information boards about the cuckoo (Gugger)
Display cases with golden eagle, chamois, mountain hare, black grouse and ibex
Kiental federal game reserve
View of the Niesen range, the Thunersee and the Wätterlatte
From Lengschwendi, a view into the upper Kiental and up to the Gamchilücke$t$),
('66b4fef91a4d9d2ffffd189b2d5a071f', 'en', $t$At the top station there's a puzzle sheet, and a small prize waits for you in the valley. From the hut to Bir Alperue it's about 1.7 km.$t$),
('9063ad590f68b7355b158e1410ad91e2', 'en', $t$Circular hike from Griesalp via the Golderli into the wide basin of the Alp Gamchi, up to Oberloch and back to Griesalp via Bundläger and the Bundalp.$t$),
('c4ea7203fda6894308997c08f6386d1e', 'en', $t$There and back: PostBus 220 to «Griesalp, Kurhaus» (late May to mid-October).
The guest card is not valid on the Kiental–Griesalp stretch.$t$),
('d8071cc100113fa1936783a279f6a8f7', 'en', $t$Small gorge above the Gamchibach
Wide basin of the Alp Gamchi
View of the Niesen from Bundläger
View into the Kiental from Dündemittelberg$t$),
('9dbc2109f0f70d8d268f6fe30611f98e', 'en', $t$Mostly mountain trail: pack hiking boots, poles, rain gear and a picnic.$t$),
('436d3473f6e8555100187b6b35dddc86', 'en', $t$Pass hike from Griesalp via the Bundalp and the Hohtürli (2778 m) to the Oeschinensee and Kandersteg, as stage 13 of the Via Alpina. The SAC's Blüemlisalphütte (2840 m) stands a few minutes above the pass.$t$),
('17cfb152544191f97e7a6b61ea7ff791', 'en', $t$June to September$t$),
('66dd4abeb20535d3e24abb05c15e7a98', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Griesalp, Kurhaus» (late May to mid-October).
Getting back: from Kandersteg with the BLS. Or take the gondola from the Oeschinensee down to Kandersteg.$t$),
('fa3c1559b31ff65214924a606fef6e31', 'en', $t$Glaciers on the north flank of the Blüemlisalp
Wooden steps along the rock face up to the Hohtürli
Blüemlisalphütte SAC a few minutes above the pass
Oeschinensee$t$),
('629d5b18e48b68b0030202ce91f41efa', 'en', $t$Above Bundläger the path gets steep and partly exposed, so you need to be sure-footed. Avoid the route in fog or snow. Snow can lie even after the route opens. Check SchweizMobil for closures before you go.$t$),
('574d16cb063000794107c04897c74aad', 'en', $t$Circular hike from Ramslauenen via the Rüederigs up the Gehrihorn (2130 m), along the ridge to the Grathütte and back to the chairlift via Bachli and Chüematti.$t$),
('9a60d713372988bdabe58771e5b9e34b', 'en', $t$There and back: PostBus 220 to «Kiental, Ramslauenen», then 15 minutes up by chairlift and back down again, free with the guest card.$t$),
('05a5856a75801e385bc3faee109ae200', 'en', $t$Summit view of the Thunersee, the Niesen range and the Kiental
View of the Blüemlisalp and the Gspaltenhorn$t$),
('8a6f3834545e0d2b3960775b4afeea80', 'en', $t$Mountain trail with a steep climb from the chairlift. You need to be sure-footed. Plan to catch the chairlift's last trip down.$t$),
('85db108cd533b919b2027dee5559ea8f', 'en', $t$Panoramic trail from Ramslauenen, high above the valley, to Griesalp at its head, past Brüggerbärgli, Gure and Mittelberg and close to the Dündefall.$t$),
('b582f55d7efacefa5d47c375c9cd2d20', 'en', $t$Late May to mid-October, on days the chairlift is running$t$),
('fd931986f3af1d312dbdbe389e60195d', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Kiental, Ramslauenen», then up by chairlift, free with the guest card.
Getting back: from «Griesalp, Kurhaus» by PostBus 220 (late May to mid-October). It also stops at «Kiental, Faulbrunni» near the hut.$t$),
('33cfba3cd8d200abadf40a052f499c16', 'en', $t$View of the Blüemlisalp range, the Tschingelsee, the Thunersee and the Niesen
Dündefall: the walkway passes close to the waterfall
Guggerwäg information boards about the cuckoo and other animals$t$),
('3254f801fc7f4c00b9482c9a072e60db', 'en', $t$There's nowhere to stop for food or drink on the way. Bring a picnic and enough to drink.$t$),
('51b0c438c746a13d27b87815f474abbf', 'en', $t$From Griesalp via Golderli, Steineberg and Bürgli into the basin of the Alp Gamchi, then over the lateral moraine of the Gamchigletscher to the SAC's Gspaltenhornhütte (2455 m). Back the same way.$t$),
('5af92e8b71dbea8d9fb19bc7893431c8', 'en', $t$July to September, when the hut is staffed$t$),
('7c71665dc7f2808e80d2b7c8bbb0256b', 'en', $t$Alpine pastures of Steineberg and Bürgli
Gamchi basin with a waterfall
Rock face with two metal bridges
Lateral moraine of the Gamchigletscher$t$),
('6371d1c279f0562e1ae52cda1a6ca992', 'en', $t$About 100 m of rocky path is secured with ropes and can be wet, so hold children by the hand. The hut belongs to the Bern section of the SAC and has 60 places.$t$),
('c40b6cce6e4128ff5b5840f37b4ebe88', 'en', $t$Pass hike over the Sefinenfurgge (2612 m) from the upper Kiental into the Lauterbrunnen valley: from Griesalp via Bürgli and Dürrebüel to the pass, down to the Rotstockhütte and via Spilboden and Gimmelen to Mürren. In the opposite direction it is stage 12 of the Via Alpina.$t$),
('30d06b7852528a8d5601d5e49033e4b6', 'en', $t$Getting there: PostBus 220 to «Griesalp, Kurhaus» (late May to mid-October).
Getting back: from «Mürren BLM» by train and cable car to Lauterbrunnen, with the BOB to Interlaken Ost, via Spiez to Reichenbach and by PostBus 220 into the Kiental. Allow a good 2 hours and several changes.$t$),
('bfe8fdb0f2197c85f03f35a06b9a0f8e', 'en', $t$Pass crossing from the Kiental into the Lauterbrunnen valley
Bryndli as a viewpoint
Mürren facing the Eiger, Mönch and Jungfrau$t$),
('10b8354abc2a691a22a3374de1f0e45f', 'en', $t$On the Kiental side, wire ropes and ladder-like steps lead steeply up to the pass. A demanding mountain hike, only for those who are sure-footed and have a head for heights.$t$),
('e0aa27127fd1dcae34607cb1ef3f5246', 'en', $t$The shortest outing from the hut: down the Guggerwäg to Bir Alperue and on to the former Tschingelsee. The picnic area by the car park on the north-west edge has fire pits for a barbecue.$t$),
('19cd9342e97a36c5f51cfecaf5609130', 'en', $t$All year round$t$),
('6aabf4f5a61775a74d4ddab12a107eb5', 'en', $t$On foot from the hut and back the same way.$t$),
('113d9ea9f8b9e9a940965ccddda504d5', 'en', $t$Floodplain with meandering streams, formed after a storm in July 1972
Waterbirds in the floodplain
From Lengschwendi, a view into the upper Kiental and up to the Gamchilücke$t$),
('8011abbac0bb8ccc9fea2a8c04dbbcda', 'en', $t$The Tschingelsee is a nature reserve and a floodplain of national importance. Fires are only allowed at the picnic area, and dogs must be on a lead. Swimming and wading are prohibited, and red and black posts close off the shore. Camping, drones, fishing and picking plants are not allowed either. Nothing says whether firewood is left at the picnic area, so it's best to bring your own. In winter, stay on the marked snowshoe route.$t$),
('50bef031fbf7d10e549ba1084e8bf28f', 'en', $t$Wooden hut on a meadow slope next to a large deciduous tree, wooded mountains with rocky peaks behind$t$),
('444692f4bd48715fd7464cf402f75632', 'en', $t$View from the hut across pasture and fir trees to snow-covered peaks$t$),
('70a3baa5052ad1089331289edb44977e', 'en', $t$Wide sleeping area with red bed linen and cushions in the sitting room, the dining table beside it$t$),
('7e8d19de19a9392ea07ff5c5efbb43c4', 'en', $t$Wood-fired stove with flue pipe and firewood, ladder to the loft, old wooden door$t$),
('eb6b0415a4916dc9d2871f925552dc6d', 'en', $t$Paved terrace with parasol, table, chair, privacy screen and outdoor fireplace$t$),
('bf1f159c73d351b01a461e82f7e22a04', 'en', $t$Hut with a solar panel on the roof, wooden fence and gravel area, a water trough in front$t$),
('5484c927ba0853c3db456bff32dbc84a', 'en', $t$Hut in summer with fenced terrace and outdoor fireplace, gravel path to the entrance$t$),
('02aa7dc312a9c4f22d07d23950efa380', 'en', $t$Side view of the hut with a woodpile and a large deciduous tree, valley and clouds behind$t$),
('32ea27a2e97ef61ded9d3c8e92cd238d', 'en', $t$Pointed snow-covered peak, bare tree and pasture with a water trough and path$t$),
('f8e908d3d176bb6936d388b4f373e83c', 'en', $t$Cup on a round garden table, behind it a wooden fence and snow-covered mountains against the light$t$),
('a71873c1149e44274ace0890b762e77e', 'en', $t$Covered wooden shelter with a bench, looking out onto a wooded slope$t$),
('08f3fa9727bef26a415008ecdb0ffc1e', 'en', $t$Sitting room with wood panelling, dining table and chairs, a bench and red and white checked curtains$t$),
('dce5d9b6f2497fa0291810bcd3bc363a', 'en', $t$Entrance room with wooden ladder to the sleeping loft, white chest of drawers and tiled floor$t$),
('a20b58804e5d04f78b5db954e655bd0d', 'en', $t$Wood-fired stove with a fire burning and the firebox door open$t$),
('6f11363c7ee2341305d467db851c7941', 'en', $t$Kitchen with stainless steel double sink, tap, cupboards and hanging cups$t$),
('4130ebdd3cad78f017d6a2b2b0c62f3b', 'en', $t$Kitchen corner with worktop, cupboards and a brick shelf, wood briquettes underneath$t$),
('2fd4858a15903df2372ffc2a766affdf', 'en', $t$Sleeping loft under the roof with mattresses, railing and light wood panelling$t$),
('031199c23fa5c61c4dc7f2be57eb3d64', 'en', $t$Corner of the entrance room with chest of drawers, lantern, orchid and wall shelf with crockery$t$),
('026a04828698b823a3806bae9316365f', 'en', $t$Wooden door of the outdoor toilet with a heart-shaped cut-out$t$),
